{"id":"CVE-2013-4073","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2013-08-18T01:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T16:30:49.912Z","description":"The OpenSSL::SSL.verify_certificate_identity function in lib/openssl/ssl.rb in Ruby 1.8 before 1.8.7-p374, 1.9 before 1.9.3-p448, and 2.0 before 2.0.0-p247 does not properly handle a '\\0' character in a domain name in the Subject Alternative Name field of an X.509 certificate, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof arbitrary SSL servers via a crafted certificate issued by a legitimate Certification Authority, a related issue to CVE-2009-2408.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2013/dsa-2738","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-2738"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-1902-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-1902-1"},{"url":"http://forums.interworx.com/threads/8000-InterWorx-Version-5-0-14-Released-on-Beta-Channel%21","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2013-1090.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2013:1090"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2013-1103.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2013:1103"},{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/security-announce/2013/Oct/msg00004.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_APPLE"],"name":"APPLE-SA-2013-10-22-3"},{"url":"http://support.apple.com/kb/HT6150","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://puppet.com/security/cve/cve-2013-4073","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=979251","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2013-07/msg00042.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2013:1181"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2013-1137.html","tags":["vendo