{"id":"CVE-2013-7295","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2014-01-17T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T18:01:20.348Z","description":"Tor before 0.2.4.20, when OpenSSL 1.x is used in conjunction with a certain HardwareAccel setting on Intel Sandy Bridge and Ivy Bridge platforms, does not properly generate random numbers for (1) relay identity keys and (2) hidden-service identity keys, which might make it easier for remote attackers to bypass cryptographic protection mechanisms via unspecified vectors.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2014-01/msg00095.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2014:0143"},{"url":"https://lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-talk/2013-December/031483.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[tor-talk] 20131223 Tor 0.2.4.20 is released"}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2013-7373","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2014-04-29T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T17:58:00.651Z","description":"Android before 4.4 does not properly arrange for seeding of the OpenSSL PRNG, which makes it easier for attackers to defeat cryptographic protection mechanisms by leveraging use of the PRNG within multiple applications.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=openssl-dev&m=130298304903422&w=2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[openssl-dev] 20110416 Re: recycled pids causes PRNG to repeat"},{"url":"http://emboss.github.io/blog/2013/08/21/openssl-prng-is-not-really-fork-safe/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://android-developers.blogspot.com.au/2013/08/some-securerandom-thoughts.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.reddit.com/r/Android/comments/1k6f03/due_to_a_serious_encryptionrng_flaw_in_android/cblvum5","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=openssl-dev&m=130289811108150&w=2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[openssl-dev] 20110415 recycled pids causes PRNG to repeat"}],"vendors":["android","openssl"]}
